WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.010
The Umbrella Academy's mind- and time-bending
finale pays off multiple plot threads that

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:09.160
have been quietly simmering in the background,
and drops a ton of new revelations that are

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.640
going to have major implications moving forward.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.480
There is no shortage of material here to unpack
and discuss.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.480
Dad the alien

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.580
Perhaps the most cryptic scene of all in The
Umbrella Academy's season finale comes right

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.110
at the beginning of the episode.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.330
It opens with a flashback: a still-living
Reginald Hargreeves is comforting a woman

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:28.779
who seems to be his lover as she dies of an
unnamed illness.

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:32.980
Outside, dozens of otherworldly spaceships
are exiting the atmosphere, indicating that

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.750
this strange world is experiencing its last
moments.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.410
Though never directly stated, we can assume
from this that Reginald Hargreeves is an alien,

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.309
something which is also briefly stated in
the comics, but not ever explored deeper.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:47.260
Also, there is one final inexplicable element.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.510
Before Reginald leaves his homeworld for Earth,
he opens a jar that releases dozens of tiny

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.610
firefly-like things which fly up into the
air and vanish.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:58.649
No explanation is given, but this is undeniably
setting up... something.

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:03.170
All we have now are tin-foil hat theories,
like the idea that there were 43 of those

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:07.969
fireflies, and these were responsible for
the 43 Earth women who gave birth to superpowered

00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:09.399
children in the first episode.

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:14.009
If this is the case, it could mean that Hargreeves
created the children as a way of giving the

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:18.170
Earth someone to protect it, as a way of atoning
for failing to protect his own homeworld.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.430
This is pure speculation of course, but it
would explain why Hargreeves was so interested

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.029
in adopting as many of these super kids as
possible.

00:01:25.029 --> 00:01:26.029
World's worst musician

00:01:26.029 --> 00:01:29.490
Once the flashback is over, we're back in
the present, where things are not going well

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.420
for what remains of the Hargreeves family.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:36.180
Vanya has discovered she has the ability to
transform ambient sound into deadly force.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.079
After getting understandably upset at her
family for — intentionally or unintentionally

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:44.009
— belittling her and deceiving her about
her powers throughout her entire life, she

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:48.499
reflexively lashes out, gravely wounding Allison
and killing several others.

00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:51.829
Up until now, the rest of the team has been
trying to figure out what's going to cause

00:01:51.829 --> 00:01:55.790
the end of the world, but now they realize
the source of the apocalypse is going to be

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:56.790
Vanya.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:00.369
"I thought Harold Jenkins was the cause, but
he was the fuse, Vanya is the bomb.

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:02.599
Vanya causes the apocalypse."

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:07.359
You see, Vanya's St. Pluvium Chamber Orchestra
has a performance later that day at the Icarus

00:02:07.359 --> 00:02:11.890
Theatre, and with her new sound manipulation
powers going out of control, this concert

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.170
has the potential to end the world.

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.170
What's with the gas masks?

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:17.890
Midway through the episode, a bunch of new
assault rifle-wielding baddies in red gas

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:20.239
masks show up and start trying to kill our
heroes.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:24.060
It's never stated explicitly where they came
from or who they're working for, but if you

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.180
were paying close attention earlier in the
season, you should recognize them instantly.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:32.349
In episode 6, those same gas masks are hanging
up in the background as the Handler is giving

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:36.659
Number Five a tour of the time travel enforcement
bureau known as the Commission.

00:02:36.659 --> 00:02:40.620
So much like Hazel, Cha Cha, and the hit squad
that attacked Number Five at the end of the

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:45.069
first episode, the men in gas masks are additional
agents in service to the Commission.

00:02:45.069 --> 00:02:49.379
The late arrival of these masked goons indicates
that we possibly haven't seen the full array

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:54.019
of the different types of agents and resources
that the Commission has at its disposal.

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:57.870
The level of threat they're going to be sending
moving forward will likely just escalate from

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:58.870
here.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:02:59.870
Hazel handles the Handler

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.890
Early in this episode, it seems Hazel might
be back to working for the wrong side.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:06.920
The Handler tells him and Cha Cha that if
they can protect Vanya until the apocalypse

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.910
hits, they'll both be forgiven for their previous
transgressions.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.590
Hazel agrees at first, but on the way to the
Icarus Theatre, things take a dramatic turn

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:19.630
when he purposefully crashes his car in an
attempt to kill Cha Cha and escape the assignment.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.189
After leaving Cha Cha for dead, Hazel returns
to the Handler's hotel room to free his girlfriend

00:03:24.189 --> 00:03:26.640
Agnes, but The Handler stands in his way.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.409
We're expecting another dramatic conversation
in which Hazel and the Handler debate the

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:34.340
merits of their respective worldviews, but
Hazel skips this part and just shoots her

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.340
in the head.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:38.599
You might think this means that his troubles
are over, but when Number Five threatened

00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:42.290
to do the same thing to the Handler in episode
five, she warned:

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:43.870
"I'll just be replaced.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:48.810
I am but a… small cog in a machine."

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.370
Even though she acts like the one directing
the entire Commission, the Handler's death

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.109
would probably only mean that things will
get worse for our heroes.

00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:58.700
Fingers crossed we'll finally get a chance
to meet the big boss from the comic book,

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:02.030
an evil sentient goldfish in a robot body
by the name of Carmichael.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.030
Klaus and Ben level up

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:07.860
During the final battle in the Icarus Theater,
Klaus exhibits a new power for the first time,

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:11.239
channeling the spirit of his dead brother
Ben, who appears in the middle of the room

00:04:11.239 --> 00:04:12.810
in a ghostly blue form.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:17.620
This manifestation of Ben is, however, quite
corporeal, as he is able to use the superpowers

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:22.000
he had when he was alive to create a mass
of super-strong tentacles to tenta-kill the

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.580
squad of Commission agents attacking his siblings.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:28.479
Klaus is able to achieve this new level of
power because he's managed to stay sober for

00:04:28.479 --> 00:04:32.430
a while now, which seems to have opened the
door to powers beyond just communicating with

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.430
the dead.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:37.530
If he remains sober into season two, we could
see Klaus use telekinesis and levitation,

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.900
a pair of powers he has in the comics, but
lacks in the show.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:45.350
It's also likely that Klaus' increased ability
to channel Ben into the physical world means

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:49.449
that the second season will give us much more
of Ben, who will also finally get a chance

00:04:49.449 --> 00:04:51.349
to interact with other members of the family.

00:04:51.349 --> 00:04:52.349
Burying the hatchet

00:04:52.349 --> 00:04:56.259
When Diego confronts Cha Cha at the Icarus,
it looks as though he'll finally be able to

00:04:56.259 --> 00:04:59.620
have his vengeance over the death of his friend,
Detective Eudora Patch.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:04.340
At the end of the fight, however, when Diego
has Cha Cha at his mercy, he ends up sparing

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.340
her life.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.069
If you were confused as to why, this is actually
a culmination of his journey throughout the

00:05:09.069 --> 00:05:10.069
season.

00:05:10.069 --> 00:05:13.870
Even before he became consumed with his quest
for revenge, Diego was always one of the morally

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.670
murkier Hargreeves children.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.460
The one thing that always kept him from going
off the deep end, however, was his friendship

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.460
with Patch.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.610
When Diego finally gets the chance to kill
Cha Cha, he can't help but imagine what Patch

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.720
would think of him now.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.919
He remembers a conversation with Five that
he had in episode nine:

00:05:28.919 --> 00:05:30.070
"Your girlfriend, Patch.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:32.129
What did you like about her?"

00:05:32.129 --> 00:05:33.280
"She believed in people.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.199
She always saw the good inside.”

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:39.949
Diego realizes that perhaps there was some
good inside Cha Cha as well, even if she herself

00:05:39.949 --> 00:05:43.460
hasn't realized it yet, and he decides to
leave her alive so maybe she can also get

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.110
a chance to find it someday.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.389
Does this mean that Diego is going to be less
broody in the future?

00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:49.610
Probably not, but it's a start.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.610
Going out with a bang

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:54.380
One of the biggest turning points in the Umbrella
Academy season 1 finale comes when Allison

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:57.300
has to decide whether or not Vanya is beyond
saving.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:01.319
Up until now, Allison has always advocated
attempting to reason with her, but when Vanya

00:06:01.319 --> 00:06:06.020
is about to kill not just the four Hargreeves
boys, but also possibly the entire world,

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:18.780
Allison realizes that she might need to be
put down for good.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:22.569
In the comics, Vanya actually does get shot
in the head at this moment, but it's Five

00:06:22.569 --> 00:06:24.639
who pulls the trigger, not Allison.

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:28.830
The comics version of Vanya ends up surviving
the injury, but she's paralyzed and suffers

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:29.830
memory loss.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:33.740
In the show, however, Allison opts for another
way, placing the gun right beside Vanya's

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.840
head and firing.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:38.680
The sound that close to Vanya's ear is enough
to break her concentration long enough for

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.639
the Hargreeves boys to escape.

00:06:40.639 --> 00:06:44.370
Even though she falls unconscious, all the
energy Vanya's been gathering up has to go

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.370
somewhere.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:49.280
As she passes out, an enormous beam of white
light erupts out of her chest and flies into

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.259
space, impacting on the full moon above.

00:06:51.259 --> 00:06:55.790
Then, as the entire moon starts to glow red
hot, it suddenly becomes very clear how the

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.160
world is supposed to end.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.870
As they say, shoot for the moon...

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:03.320
As pieces of the moon rain down from the heavens,
our heroes only have a few moments to do something

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:04.449
to save the world.

00:07:04.449 --> 00:07:05.449
How do they manage it?

00:07:05.449 --> 00:07:06.610
Well, they don't.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:10.159
Number Five makes them all gather together
so they can travel back in time to try and

00:07:10.159 --> 00:07:12.050
prevent the apocalypse at an earlier juncture.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:14.340
"I think I have a way outta here.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.919
But you've gotta trust me on this."

00:07:16.919 --> 00:07:17.919
"No…"

00:07:17.919 --> 00:07:21.409
The long term-consequences on Vanya aren't
clear, since she passes out immediately and

00:07:21.409 --> 00:07:25.580
doesn't wake up before the end of the episode,
but it's possible she's suffered hearing damage.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:29.500
That would certainly make her career as a
violinist more difficult, and add an unexpected

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.949
wrinkle to a character with the ability to
control sound.

00:07:31.949 --> 00:07:32.949
Time travel, killers, and the future

00:07:32.949 --> 00:07:36.670
We can assume that very few people survive
the end of the world, outside of our main

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:40.080
seven heroes — if you can count Ben as "surviving,"
that is.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:44.509
Most of the other named characters were dead
already, including Pogo, Mom, Leonard, and

00:07:44.509 --> 00:07:45.509
the Handler.

00:07:45.509 --> 00:07:46.919
But what about Hazel and Cha Cha?

00:07:46.919 --> 00:07:51.129
It's a blink and you'll miss it moment, but
a second before the blast hits Hazel and Agnes,

00:07:51.129 --> 00:07:53.129
they disappear in a flash of blue light.

00:07:53.129 --> 00:07:57.099
This implies they stole a Briefcase — one
of the Commission's time travel devices — from

00:07:57.099 --> 00:07:58.689
the Handler after killing her.

00:07:58.689 --> 00:08:02.409
We don't know where Hazel and Agnes traveled
to, but we can assume we haven't seen the

00:08:02.409 --> 00:08:03.409
last of them.

00:08:03.409 --> 00:08:05.310
Cha Cha's fate is far more grim.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:09.660
Despite technically succeeding at her final
assignment of keeping Vanya Hargreeves alive,

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:14.669
we see that in her final moments, she is trying
and failing to contact HQ from a payphone.

00:08:14.669 --> 00:08:18.660
This could be because, as Hazel predicted,
the Commission never intended to rescue them

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:22.530
from the apocalypse, or it could simply be
because the Handler is dead, and there's no

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:23.870
one to receive her call.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:27.400
Either way, we unfortunately have to say "ta
ta" to Cha Cha.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:31.169
But, since Hazel and Cha Cha have had long
and illustrious careers as time-traveling

00:08:31.169 --> 00:08:34.980
assassins, it's possible that the Hargreeves
will run into these two again at an earlier

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:38.180
point in their lives, when the pair were still
cold-blooded killers.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:40.630
Nothing can mess with a character arc quite
like time travel.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:43.980
"The old man did say time travel could contaminate
the mind."

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:45.430
Umbrella Academy babies?

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:48.960
As the Hargreeves are preparing to travel
back in time, they appear for a moment to

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.150
be de-aged back to how they looked as teenagers.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:55.480
It is possible that this is just supposed
to be a cool, artsy way to end the season,

00:08:55.480 --> 00:09:00.480
a symbolic representation of how the Hargreeves
have finally been reunited together as a family,

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.970
like back when they were children.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:05.830
But it's also possible that this moment is
meant to be taken very literally.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:08.340
Remember that Number Five himself didn't always
look 13.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:13.370
He used to be a 58-year-old man, but his age
was reset back to 13 as an unintended side

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.770
effect of the method he used to time travel.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:19.750
If Five is sending his siblings back using
the same method, it's possible that they'll

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.500
be de-aged the same way he was.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.250
From what we've seen of Five's struggles with
this situation, getting stuck in a body that's

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:29.090
the wrong age is not an easy problem to fix.

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:33.070
"It's been a rough couple of days."

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:36.600
If this does indeed happen, then a big conflict
for the coming season will probably be the

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.110
team trying to find a way to return to adulthood.

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:43.650
There might be another side effect to this,
however, and it's more unambiguously positive.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:47.710
Since Ben's ghost is also hitching a ride,
if everything about these characters is reversing

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:51.470
to how things were when they were teens, it's
possible that he might not just be returned

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:53.920
to youth, but back to life as well.

